    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for LawDog today centers on **Bryce Harper** (66.83) and **Cal Raleigh** (64.55), who stand as our premier starts. **Bryce Harper** benefits from a high-leverage #3 spot against Mahle, where his xwOBA and park factors coalesce into an elite daily efficiency score. Similarly, **Cal Raleigh** remains a top-tier play; despite a moderate xERA from the opposing arm, his power profile is bolstered by a favorable platoon split and an anchor spot at #4 in the lineup. **Luis Arraez** also presents a stable floor near 60, leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Mahle to maintain our target AVG metrics.\n\nEfficiency gaps across the outfield and middle infield remain tight, leading to a difficult bench decision regarding **Jonathan Aranda**. With a score of 46.70, **Jonathan Aranda** was the final omission; while he carries an attractive #2 spot in the lineup, his negative dynamic platoon split against the left-handed Gore ultimately pushed him below the threshold set by the higher-floor profiles of **Braden Montgomery** (52.86) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (52.15). We are keeping a close watch on **Will Smith** and **Alex Freeland**, as their scores are based on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; if either shifts down the order, we may need to pivot. Furthermore, while **Daulton Varsho** (52.27) faces a pitcher with a 4.65 xERA, his effectiveness is dampened by a negative platoon split, though we remain optimistic given the higher stolen base potential against a slower delivery.\n\nRisk management is a priority today, specifically regarding **Zack Gelof** (43.74) and **JJ Bleday** (47.86). **Zack Gelof** faces a stiff challenge against Woo\u2019s 3.56 xERA, making him a marginal play that we are monitoring closely to protect our category caps. While the rest of the roster\u2014including **Lawrence Butler** and the speed-heavy **Justin Crawford**\u2014are positioned to contribute to our scarcity-driven targets, the path to a 90+ efficiency day is narrow given the quality of opposing arms like Woo and Harrison. We have confirmed that **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Tyler Freeman** remain unavailable, leaving our current configuration as the most statistically sound approach to defending our Roto standing.",
